# PraHari — Docker build context exclusions
#
# Without this file the ENTIRE repository is sent to the Docker daemon as
# build context — including prahari.db, which holds genuine local network
# telemetry (local and remote addresses, ports, owning process ids). None
# of it is needed to build the image, and a build context is trivially
# recoverable from a daemon or a CI log.
#
# The COPY instructions in the Dockerfile are narrow, so this data would
# not reach the final image; it would still leave the machine.

# ── Telemetry and secrets: never, under any circumstances ──
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
secrets/
credentials.json
*credentials*.json
experiments/
.env
.env.*

# ── Version control and history ──
.git/
.gitignore
.github/

# ── Build outputs and caches (rebuilt inside the image) ──
node_modules/
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
backend/.venv/
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# ── Tests and docs: not needed at runtime ──
backend/tests/
docs/
*.md
!README.md

# ── Editor and OS noise ──
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log

# ── Local tooling ──
.claude/
scripts/__pycache__/

# ── Research corpora and local data (added for benchmark readiness) ──
# Benchmark CSVs are large third-party artefacts with their own licence and
# attribution terms. They are never committed: the repository would carry
# redistributed data, and a multi-hundred-megabyte file would be in every
# clone forever. Small synthetic fixtures written BY the test suite are not
# affected — they live in temporary directories, not here.
# Root-anchored on purpose. An unanchored `research/` would match
# backend/app/research/ — the source package — and silently hide it from
# version control. Verified with `git check-ignore`.
/research/
/research-data/
/datasets/
/data/raw/
/data/corpora/
*.pcap
*.pcapng

# Local CSV data. Deliberately scoped so documentation, source and small
# committed fixtures are untouched; only the data drop locations above and
# top-level stray CSVs are excluded.
/*.csv
/backend/*.csv
/frontend/*.csv

# Research import manifests sit beside the research database and record
# local filenames and hashes.
manifests/
